Ready-Made Website

A ready-made website is a website that is already designed and built using a template, theme, or website builder. You do not need to create everything from scratch.

You mainly select, customize, and add your own content or features.

Examples

| Platform      | How it works                        |
| ------------- | ----------------------------------- |
| **WordPress** | Select a theme and customize pages  |
| **Elementor** | Drag-and-drop website design        |
| **Wix**       | Ready-made website templates        |
| **Shopify**   | Ready-made e-commerce website       |
| **Webflow**   | Templates with visual customization |


Example: Hospital Website + CKD Application

Suppose you already have a ready-made hospital website:

Hospital Website
│
├── Home
├── About Us
├── Services
├── Doctors
├── Contact
└── CKD Prediction  ← Add this page


===


The CKD application is separately deployed:

CKD Flask Application
        │
        ▼
Public URL
        │
        ▼
https://your-ckd-app-url

Then add that URL to the ready-made website using an HTML/Embed widget or iframe:

===

<iframe
    src="YOUR_CKD_APP_PUBLIC_URL"
    width="100%"
    height="800"
    style="border: none;">
</iframe>

